# TextFSM template: Cisco IOS / IOS-XE `ping`.
#
# IOS's ping is terse compared to iputils: one progress-marker line
# (`!!!!!`) followed by a single summary line. There is no per-probe
# breakdown and no jitter (mdev) figure — those fields end up zero.
#
# Sample output (success):
#   Type escape sequence to abort.
#   Sending 5, 100-byte ICMP Echos to 1.1.1.1, timeout is 2 seconds:
#   Packet sent with a source address of 10.0.0.1
#   !!!!!
#   Success rate is 100 percent (5/5), round-trip min/avg/max = 1/2/4 ms
#
# Sample output (total loss):
#   Sending 5, 100-byte ICMP Echos to 10.255.255.1, timeout is 2 seconds:
#   .....
#   Success rate is 0 percent (0/5)
#
# IOS reports the success *rate*; we derive loss_pct = 100 - success.
# packets_received is `(received/sent)` so we capture both numerator
# and denominator and let the projector consume both. The RTT line
# is optional (absent on 0% success) so we land on Record either way.
Value Required target (\S+)
Value source (\S+)
Value packets_sent (\d+)
Value packets_received (\d+)
Value loss_pct (\d+(?:\.\d+)?)
Value rtt_min_ms (\d+(?:\.\d+)?)
Value rtt_avg_ms (\d+(?:\.\d+)?)
Value rtt_max_ms (\d+(?:\.\d+)?)

Start
  ^Sending\s+\d+,\s+\d+-byte\s+ICMP\s+Echos\s+to\s+${target},
  ^Packet\s+sent\s+with\s+a\s+source\s+address\s+of\s+${source}
  ^Success\s+rate\s+is\s+(?P<_success>\d+)\s+percent\s+\(${packets_received}/${packets_sent}\)(?:,\s+round-trip\s+min/avg/max\s+=\s+${rtt_min_ms}/${rtt_avg_ms}/${rtt_max_ms}\s+ms)? -> Record
